    "question": {
      ":question/id": "798aa69f-3160-52d6-bb18-6a33212fc3d9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $4\\times 5$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $1$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 1+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-1 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
